          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.2.3 Velocity-time graphs"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.107,
            0.111,
            0.776,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The velocity-time graph of an object in motion represents the change in its velocity with time. In a manner similar to the position-time graph, you can plot velocity-time graphs following the steps of Activity 4.3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.166,
            0.51,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us take the example of a car moving in the same direction on a straight stretch of a highway at a steady velocity of 72 km "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { h } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 0 \\; \\mathrm { { m } \\; s ^ { - 1 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The velocity-time graph corresponding to it is shown in Fig. 4.17a."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.253,
            0.509,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider another car that starts moving from rest and its velocity increases with time as shown in Table 4.5. The velocity-time graph plotted for this case is shown in Fig. 4.17b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.341,
            0.509,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider yet another car moving with a velocity of 15.0 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { S } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Its velocity decreases with time as shown in Table 4.6 and its velocity-time graph is shown in Fig. 4.17c."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
